hi there steve kaufman here and as you  know i like to talk about language  learning if you enjoy my channel please  subscribe  and i try to put out a video at least  once a week on  tips or  uh experience that i have had in  learning up to 15 languages today i'm  going to talk about what i think is a  very important quality in any language  learner and that is patience  patience and unfortunately most language  learners don't have patience they want  quick results  learning a language is actually changing  habits in your brain it takes time i  sometimes think that these techniques  that people use like spaced repetition  systems or studying long vocabulary  lists or even to some extent this focus  on grammar  is an attempt to short circuit a process  which actually takes a long time and it  takes a lot of exposure a lot of reading  and listening and eventually speaking in  order to create new habits  and it it is a matter of habits i was  talking to a an american who has been  teaching english in china and i asked  him what are the main difficulties that  chinese people have in english  and he said three he said first of all  the the third person singular the  present tense like he goes instead of he  go and that's common not only for  chinese speakers but for for lots of  people particularly if it's you know the  car that it was parked beside the school  is you have to remember that it's in  fact it's the only you know  call it ending with an s in other words  i go you go he goes we go they go  you go  so and it just seems even though that's  easy to explain it takes so long to get  used to  the second difficulty chinese people had  was he and she  because in chinese in spoken chinese  there's no difference between he and she  you just pick it up from the context but  in english there is easy concept easily  explained everybody understands it and  after five ten years chinese people will  still say you know they get about a  fifty percent  success rate my husband she i know my  husband he because you have to create  that habit  the other difficult the chinese people  had was with plurals because they don't  really have plurals in their nouns but  it's the same for uh english speakers  speaking languages where they have  gender if we don't have gender in  english so it takes a long time to get  used to  getting the gender right  we just default to le in french  people who have gender in their own  languages have an easier time learn  learning the gender of nouns in other  languages where they have gender  um  people who speak languages where they  have no articles they have all kinds of  trouble with articles  in english or in french or spanish  languages which have articles it just  takes time  i enjoyed uh fact i put a link there was  a  russian program called easy russian  where this the teacher there says throw  away the grammar book i wouldn't go that  far but don't rely on  the ability to kind of deduce the  grammar as a shortcut to learning the  language even if you understand the  explanation which is not always a given  you still have to put in that time of  listening and reading to create some new  habits so that gradually the brain  starts to create these patterns which  enables the brain then on the fly while  you're speaking to produce the language  correctly the same is true for people  who say i still don't understand i don't  understand movies i don't understand  this i was at a with a group of people  last night i didn't feel that i spoke as  well as i should and all this kind of  stuff  it takes time the language remains fuzzy  you're still stuck in old habits and  it's only through  a lot of exposure that you're going to  form new habits so  i just there's nothing wrong with some  of these other aids to learning if you  enjoy doing them  but if you think that's going to  short-circuit the system enable you to  to suddenly speak well or understand  well i don't think so perhaps some  people but that's certainly not my  experience so i recommend that people be  patient  when they learn languages and keep at it  and you will eventually improve  and if you enjoy hearing about language  learning  please subscribe to my channel  bye and thanks for listening
 

